  "strict_feasibility": {
    "definitions": {
      "why": "The trainer's Genesis criterion tests the MEDIAN relative balance residual over the independent rows of S. A flux vector that is zero on most reactions passes that test on the zeros alone: the median row of a mostly-off vector has no production to fail to consume. The max over the same rows is the honest form of 'this vector balances', and the fraction of reactions carrying flux says whether there was anything to balance.",
      "balance_max_ratio": "max over the independent rows i of S of |(Sv)_i| / (omega_i + balance_epsilon), the same ratio the trainer takes the median of. Computed by train_bx._per_sample_feasibility, which every wave-6 cell already recorded the distribution of; only the CRITERION built on it is new.",
      "flux_active_frac": "fraction of the 4,131 reactions with |v| > 1e-6 * flux_scale = 1e-4 mmol/gDW/h.",
      "genesis_median_rule": "the trainer's criterion: balance_median_ratio <= 1e-2 AND no active reaction running uphill at standard state.",
      "genesis_max_rule": "the same criterion with balance_max_ratio <= 1e-2 in place of the median, so EVERY independent row must balance, not the typical one.",
      "balance_active_max_ratio_<t>": "max of the same ratio over the independent rows whose turnover omega_i exceeds t * flux_scale. The plain max is decided by rows at the balance_epsilon floor, where two tiny same-sign fluxes give a ratio of exactly 2, so it fails every head for a reason unrelated to the flux the model carries; restricting to rows that turn over is the rule that separates the heads.",
      "balance_active_p95_ratio_<t>": "the 95th percentile of the same ratio over the same rows, which is the max with the top 5 percent of rows removed and is what a handful of near-threshold rows cannot dominate.",
      "balance_active_rows_<t>": "how many independent rows clear the turnover threshold. A rule evaluated over three rows is not a statement about the flux vector, so the count is reported beside every thresholded ratio.",
      "genesis_active_rule": "the Genesis criterion with balance_active_max_ratio at the primary threshold (1e-3 * flux_scale) <= 1e-2 in place of the median or the plain max."
    },
